ritical string become tensionless at finite distance while a transverse gauge coupling remains finite? The authors question whether its non-BPS particle excitations actually form an infinite massless tower.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0031"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:8945df99f654a968d79d221840576b69721be9bf16e73a25a7f2199435b9c300","title":"Can monodromy enlarge ALP misalignment production enough to allow stronger couplings while retaining viable dark matter, and how do resonantly amplified nonlinear fluctuations affect abundance, velocities and small-scale density structure?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0039"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:89d2693724352c8179da6dc619ad979464a5ff314bcfe4e56ba0e517d9382773","title":"Can radial and angular motion of a wrapped probe D5-brane realize the all-heavy, rapidly turning inflationary mechanism?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0044"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:8910cd688c793cba953d7b2d908791b4a94ff808e67d553ec39bc3d47126279a","title":"Does the first bosonic Higuchi excursion constraint have a substantive connection to the spin-2 conjecture? How does curvature modify the Regge spectrum when the string scale changes exponentially? Both questions are explicitly deferred rather than answered.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0048"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:89532602eae3619289935e8e286f7892edd6592c8185ed8d90a66f69c92327d5","title":"Can another eight-dimensional construction with 16 supercharges realize E8+D7+A3, and could global anomalies explain why this algebra is excluded in toroidal heterotic compactification?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0055"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:89495094b88ea698d525257093a