ructure more concrete, and clarify the cobordism conjecture's gravity-decoupling limit?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0073"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:89d534235583f09c1eaae39379028fcc8b97d5ae5635de7315cbf9200a954cd0","title":"Can gauge theories possess conserved time-reversal operators beyond the familiar invertible symmetries at special θ, and how do discrete higher-form gauging, fusion and counterterms determine their noninvertible realizations?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0076"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:89f0b59a9cef3644f036e410054a5ec7d8ae08c8b320cc48e3aa405c89107485","title":"How does antibrane uplift correlate with towers of states across strong and weak warping, and what constraints follow for a reliable EFT and its superpotential?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0081"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:89409c410ba6f06089a6ca9b2497fc8c3b5fc13d3bbf5cb4f704055f6d782a61","title":"Can local, nontrivial cancellation of twisted R-R charges produce BSB orientifolds with fewer brane deformation moduli, and how should their gauge kinetic functions and string-defect unitarity constraints be formulated?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0087"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:894e4616b85c34a597c26645d9147e47bb48b4730f21b11341275811aad000b1","title":"Can higher-order flux-superpotential terms stabilize fields that remain massless at quadratic order in the 1^9 Landau–Ginzburg model, and how does this distinction affect tadpole bounds? A parallel aim is completing the classification of fluxes with minimal tadpole contribution.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0088"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:8926eb3f599906376134ec16b188a58ea369408d1806948242f4e705a8aaa375"